    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe requirement: alongside the existing human-readable audit line, emit an immutable structured JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**1. New immutable event type** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (a Java `record`, so all fields are final and the instance can't be mutated after construction). Its components serialize in the spec's order: `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`. A factory `of(seq, ownerId, primaryIdentifier, membershipLevel)` sets `event` to the `OWNER_CREATED` marker and takes the primary identifier as its own parameter.\n\n**2. Wiring in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:**\n- A static `AtomicInteger OWNER_CREATE_SEQUENCE` \u2014 a **monotonically increasing sequence shared across all creates** (across requests/threads); the first event is `seq=1`.\n- A static Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) `ObjectMapper` to serialize the event.\n- A new `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)` called right after the existing audit line, emitting e.g.:\n  ```json\n  {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n  ```\n\n**Honoring the forward-looking requirement:** the event is designed to carry the owner's *current primary identifier*, not a hard-coded notion of \"customer code.\" `emitOwnerCreatedEvent` passes `owner.getCustomerCode()` as the `primaryIdentifier` argument. When the customer code is later unified into a `memberId`, only that one argument changes to `owner.getMemberId()` and the event automatically carries the new identifier \u2014 the event type and emission logic stay untouched.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier`) confirms one `AUDIT` line contains the `OWNER_CREATED` marker, the owner id, and the customer code.",
